{:type :principle
 :id :principle/propagator-fixpoint-evaluation
 :text "Fixpoint evaluation: Repeated local propagation refines information toward quiescence under the domain information order. Updates are monotone in that order, and merge is associative, commutative and idempotent under domain-defined semantic equality. Order-independent outcomes require compatible monotone rules and fair scheduling; termination additionally requires suitable convergence conditions. These are semantic requirements, not a claim that every implementation or arbitrary recursive network has been proved convergent."
 :created-at #inst "2026-10-18T14:56:25.000Z"
 :source "user-request:append-four-semantic-principles:2026-10-18"
