{:type :principle
 :id :principle/propagator-partial-information
 :text "Partial information: A cell can hold incomplete, structured, conditional or conflicting knowledge rather than a single ground value. Merge combines contributions according to the information domain; strongest is a derived readable projection distinct from retained content. Preserve live slot/accessor relationships so later refinements propagate through structure. Evidence compaction must follow the explicit domain order rather than assuming a particular set representation."
 :created-at #inst "2026-10-18T14:56:25.000Z"
 :source "user-request:append-four-semantic-principles:2026-10-18"
 :scope "Information policy / compound partial-information structure"
