{:type :principle
 :id :principle/propagator-dependence-tracking
 :text "Dependence tracking: Retain the justifications on which conclusions depend, and use domain-owned support and retraction semantics to determine which conclusions remain warranted. Dependency identity and validity come from information contributions, not the scheduler execution history. A retraction can change the readable conclusion while domain evidence is accumulated or compacted according to its information order. Existing TTMS and distributed TMS are explicit mechanisms, not proof of a universal dependence subsystem."
 :created-at #inst "2026-10-18T14:56:25.000Z"
 :source "user-request:append-four-semantic-principles:2026-10-18"
